📌 LV Automation – Simplifying Sanity Checks in Production
🔍 Problem Statement (Before Automation)
In the current setup, RMs perform LV sanity checks manually in production.

This involves navigating the application, validating major screens, and capturing screenshots.

The process is time-consuming and error-prone, taking 30–40 minutes per CR per market.

Screens are verified manually, and there’s no structured report or audit trail.

✅ Our Solution: LV Automation
We have implemented a secure, fully automated LV verification pipeline triggered via Jenkins in production:

Automation is triggered by providing a username and test data file.

The pipeline is reviewed and approved by EASRE to ensure:

No sensitive data is printed to the console

Full security compliance

Reports are audit-ready

🔐 Secure & Actionable Output
On execution, the respective RM receives:

An email notification

A password-protected ZIP file containing:

HTML screenshots

A detailed execution report

A video recording of the entire automation

The video allows RM to review the run visually without re-executing anything manually.

⏱️ Results & Efficiency Gains
For SG market: 95 test steps executed in just 5 minutes.

Manual time: ~30–40 mins ➝ Now: 5 mins

Time saved per run: ~25–35 minutes

